# Committed deliberately: NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined into the browser bundle at
# build time, so this value is public either way. Keeping it here rather than in
# a CI dashboard means the value travels with the source.
#
# The /api/v1 suffix is required; a bare host 404s at the gateway.
#
# How /api/v1/platform/* resolves — verified against the running backend
# 2026-09-02, superseding an earlier note here that called it unknown:
#
#   1. Caddy has a dedicated `handle /api/v1/platform/*` block that reverse
#      proxies to auth-service:8081. It is separate from the /api/v1/auth/*
#      block because Caddy `handle` blocks are mutually exclusive prefix
#      matches, so the auth rule does not cover it. Rate limited to 10 req/min
#      per client IP (tighter than college auth — this is a single account).
#   2. auth-service registers the routes in internal/routes/routes.go, guarded
#      by `if utils.PlatformAuthEnabled()`, i.e. only when PLATFORM_JWT_SECRET
#      is set. Without that secret the whole platform surface is absent and
#      every path here 404s.
#
# The registered surface, all of which this console calls:
#   POST   /platform/auth/login
#   GET    /platform/auth/me
#   PUT    /platform/auth/password
#   GET    /platform/stats                     → bare stats object
#   GET    /platform/audit                     → { entries: [...] }
#   GET|POST    /platform/colleges             → { colleges: [...] }
#   PUT|DELETE  /platform/colleges/:id
#   GET    /platform/colleges/:id/stats
#   POST   /platform/colleges/:id/activate | /deactivate | /impersonate
#   GET|POST    /platform/colleges/:id/admins
#   DELETE /platform/colleges/:id/admins/:userId
#
# There is NO platform refresh endpoint, and PlatformLogin returns no refresh
# token — the access token is deliberately short-lived (8h). src/lib/api.ts
# carries the renewal path anyway; it stays inert until the service issues one.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.twincord.in/api/v1
